/// The model list, for the model manager's window (P4 task 10): the stored and
/// signed models, the one in use, the next restart's and the last trial, each
/// signed one with its licence. Like `kai:system`, this is a granted interface,
/// not part of `kai:app` (which is frozen): only the app the system image names
/// `models-window` holds the `models` grant, and a component that imports it
/// without the grant does not stage (`Reason::Link`).
///
/// `read` only queues. The host takes the queue after the call, asks the update
/// service for its list, and tells the app the answer in a later call, so a call
/// never waits on the system, and a version rehearsed beside the active one
/// cannot read twice: only the shown version's queue is taken. The answer is the
/// list as `kai-models 1` text, at most one IPC message (8 KiB); the app parses
/// it as it would any input, and a list it cannot parse is one it does not show.
///
/// Since 0.1.1 the window may also switch the model itself on a person's key or
/// click (#556), as the Settings app changes a setting: `use-model` queues the
/// switch, which goes to the shell, which runs Kai's own `model_use` row with the
/// person's consent, logged, and undone by `undo`. An import still goes through
/// Kai or the console, where it asks on the trusted path.
package kai:models@0.1.1;

interface models {
    /// Asks for the list and returns its ticket. Refused (the call traps) when 4
    /// reads are waiting for the host already.
    read: func() -> u32;

    /// Asks for the stored model with this SHA-256 (64 lowercase hex digits) to
    /// be the one the next restart uses, on trial, and returns the request's
    /// ticket. It is passed on only when a person's key or click made it, and a
    /// call may make one; any other is answered with why not. The call traps for
    /// a SHA-256 that is not 64 lowercase hex digits, or when 4 switches are
    /// waiting for the host already.
    @since(version = 0.1.1)
    use-model: func(sha256: string) -> u32;
}

/// What the update service and the shell answered.
interface listing {
    /// The answer to the read with this ticket: the list, or why there is none
    /// (no model store, or the service did not answer; at most 200 printable
    /// ASCII bytes). A ticket is not reused while this instance runs; a new
    /// instance starts again from 0.
    on-listing: func(ticket: u32, outcome: result<string, string>);

    /// The answer to the switch with this ticket: what the shell said it did,
    /// or why it did not. Tickets count on their own, apart from the reads'.
    @since(version = 0.1.1)
    on-used: func(ticket: u32, outcome: result<string, string>);
}

/// An app that reads the model list and, since 0.1.1, switches the model on a
/// person's key: the two halves of the grant.
world models-read {
    import models;
    export listing;
}
